                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Good and Challenging game!\n\nThe Game is about freefalling in space or in narrow corridors. It has 3 modes in 3 difficulty settings, which you can cycle through in the title screen with Q and E.\n[list]\n[*] The easiest is the Green, where you are freefalling in empty space while avoiding obstacles.\n[*] The medium is the Blue where the obstacles tend to expand after a while and form narrow corridors in a maze like structure.\n[*] The hardest is the Red where, like in Green, you are freefalling in emty space with obstacles, however you are gravitated towards the nearest obstacle and you need to change directions in order to oppose the gravitational forces and avoid collisions.\n[/list]\n\nIt has enough video options, like Detail level, Bloom, cel-shaded, grain filtering, voxel setting, yet it lacks resolution and fullscreen options.\n\nPerformance wise it can perform above 30 FPS. On my A8-5550 APU with an integated 8650M (laptop)  I got around 30 FPS on the third detail level with bloom and cell-shaded on. If I turned anything off or lowered the detail level I got a consistent increase of 5 FPS for each setting lowered",
